  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all incidents and 48-hour customer notice. S2 sets a 7% permanent failure cap (above the 5% safe limit) with review above 5%, but requires per-model failure rates to be given to customers while not publishing them publicly. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 36 months and retrofit to 6 years with a feasibility escape; S5 makes the 8/100k threshold a trigger for regulator review and possible corrective action rather than a mandatory recall."
